@@ -1177,11 +1177,11 @@ msgid "Show the internal disks (read-only)"
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#32923"
-msgid "Off (the default): run from a USB drive, this system does not see the disks inside the computer; installed on one of them, it does not see the other disks and does not mount the rest of its own. On: from the next start they are all mounted read-only, and the kernel runs without its lockdown. This makes the entry of the boot menu that shows the internal disks the one that starts by itself; choosing \"run\" in that menu once turns it off again."
+msgid "Off (the default): run from a USB drive, this system does not see the disks inside the computer; installed on one of them, it does not see the other disks and does not mount the rest of its own. On: from the next start they are mounted read-only (all their partitions, or the ones chosen below), and the kernel runs without its lockdown. This makes the entry of the boot menu that shows the internal disks the one that starts by itself; choosing \"run\" in that menu once turns it off again."
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#32924"
-msgid "With this setting on, from the next start:[CR][CR]- This system sees the disks inside the computer and mounts them read-only: all of them when it runs from a USB drive; when it is installed on one of them, the other disks and the other partitions of its own disk. That is where Windows and your files are.[CR][CR]- Everything that runs here can read them: the media centre and every add-on, also the ones made by other people. With file sharing (Samba) turned on, they can be shared on your network too.[CR][CR]- \"Read-only\" is how the disks are mounted, not a lock. Add-ons run with full rights: one that wanted to could mount them again for writing.[CR][CR]- The kernel runs without its lockdown. In the normal start it loads only the drivers that came with this system and keeps programs away from the memory and the hardware of the computer. In this one it does neither.[CR][CR]- It is so on every computer that this drive is started on.[CR][CR]It stays on until you turn it off here, reset this system to its defaults, or choose \"run\" once in the menu that is shown when the computer starts (on a UEFI computer that entry is \"Run\", not the one that names the internal disks). An update made with the installer for Windows turns it off as well."
+msgid "With this setting on, from the next start:[CR][CR]- This system sees the disks inside the computer and mounts them read-only: all of them when it runs from a USB drive; when it is installed on one of them, the other disks and the other partitions of its own disk. That is where Windows and your files are.[CR][CR]- Everything that runs here can read them: the media centre and every add-on, also the ones made by other people. With file sharing (Samba) turned on, they can be shared on your network too.[CR][CR]- \"Read-only\" is how the disks are mounted, not a lock. Add-ons run with full rights: one that wanted to could mount them again for writing.[CR][CR]- Below this setting you can choose partitions that stay hidden: they are not mounted, but a program that runs here with full rights could still read them.[CR][CR]- The kernel runs without its lockdown. In the normal start it loads only the drivers that came with this system and keeps programs away from the memory and the hardware of the computer. In this one it does neither.[CR][CR]- It is so on every computer that this drive is started on.[CR][CR]It stays on until you turn it off here, reset this system to its defaults, or choose \"run\" once in the menu that is shown when the computer starts (on a UEFI computer that entry is \"Run\", not the one that names the internal disks). An update made with the installer for Windows turns it off as well."
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#32925"
@@ -1459,3 +1459,63 @@ msgstr ""
 msgctxt "#33120"
 msgid "%s did not accept the key saved for it. Pair it again."
 msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33130"
+msgid "Internal partitions that are shown"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33131"
+msgid "Which partitions of the internal disks are mounted, read-only, while the setting above shows them. One that is not chosen is not mounted at all: Kodi, its add-ons and file sharing do not see it. It is still in the computer, though: a program that runs here with full rights could read it all the same, so to keep every internal disk out of reach, turn the setting above off. Partitions are told apart by the serial number of their disk and the identifier of the partition, not by names such as sda1, which can change from one start to the next. A choice holds from the next start."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33132"
+msgid "Any partition that is not in this list (a new one, another disk, another PC)"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33133"
+msgid "No name"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33134"
+msgid "%s (%s, %s), on %s, now %s"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33135"
+msgid "serial number ending in %s"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33136"
+msgid "a disk"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33137"
+msgid "%s: not connected in this start"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33138"
+msgid "In this start the internal disks are hidden, so their partitions cannot be listed. With the setting above on, they are shown from the next start: restart the system, then choose them here."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33139"
+msgid "No internal partition that could be shown was found in this start."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33140"
+msgid "These partitions cannot be told apart from others (their disk has no serial number, or the partition has no identifier), so they go with the first line of the list, the one for any partition that is not in it: %s"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33141"
+msgid "The list of the partitions that are shown could not be read, so no internal partition is mounted. Choose them again to make a new list."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33142"
+msgid "The partitions are shown as chosen from the next start"
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33143"
+msgid "The list could not be saved, so the partitions are shown as before. Try again; if it keeps failing, restart the system first."
+msgstr ""
+
+msgctxt "#33144"
+msgid "The partitions of the internal disks could not be listed."
+msgstr ""
